---
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<section id="how-ai" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16">
	<div class="max-w-[62ch]">
		<h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">How the AI on this page works</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
			This is a static page. The fit check at the top and the question box in the FAQ send your text and the page's own copy to
			<a href="https://onetagai.com/?ref=astro-ai-landing" class="underline underline-offset-2">OneTag AI</a> from your browser; the answer is written from this page and nothing else.
			There is no server behind {site.name}'s site, no account, and nothing you type is stored. Site owners add one script tag and a public key; the template is
			<a href="https://github.com/fengyiqicoder/astro-ai-landing" class="underline underline-offset-2">open source</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>
